are  popped  off  the stack; the result is pushed on the stack in
their place.  Any fractional part of an exponent is ignored.  For
addition and subtraction, the scale of the result is the  maximum
of  scales of the operands.  For division the scale of the result
is defined by the scale set by the  operation.   For  multiplica‐
